# Force LF everywhere, regardless of the checkout platform's core.autocrlf.
# Without this, a Windows commit of throughline/web (built by `npm run build`,
# then compared byte-for-byte by CI's "Frontend build is current" check) picks
# up CRLF from `core.autocrlf=true`, and a fresh Linux build in CI emits LF for
# the same file, which reads as the committed build being stale even when it
# is not.
* text=auto eol=lf
